<title>UK: Pillar buys shopping centre from L&amp;G.</title>
<headline>Pillar buys shopping centre from L&amp;G.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>PillarCaisse, a joint venture between Pillar Property Investments and Canada's La Caisse, has bought a shopping centre in Mansfield, northern England, for 23.75 million stg from Legal &amp; General.  </p>
<p>The Four Seasons shopping centre comprises 21,500 square metres of retail space made up of 60 units.</p>
<p>&quot;The purchase of this very sound property located on Mansfield's main shopping pitch strengthens our portfolio, with an opportunity to improve the centre through refurbishment,&quot; said PillarCaisse's chief executive Simon Winslow.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7717</p>
